Mild spoilers follow.

Ludios is good for:

1) Large piles of weapons and armor for polypiling (and if you go to
the effort of polypiling all the bugles, chests, and disarmed mines, a
few tools too).

2) Food

3) Dragon scale, which you don't need

4) Dragon meat, if you really need a resistance or two

5) A throne

6) A big pile of gold

7) Some good gems

8) If you have the eye, it's a convenient portal point if you want to
set up a base in the branch level.

9) A bunch of wands.

IMHO, 80 hp is pretty low to do the castle, where you're likely to get
an L or two, but if you're comfortable and don't want Ludios's gold and
gems, you can easily skip Ludios.


